Clinical Course: The bleeding has completely stopped and the wound is securely closed. You will experience a dull ache tonight as the local anesthetic wears off.
SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE
Seek immediate medical attention if you lose feeling in your fingers or if bright red streaks begin spreading up your arm from the wound site.
PATIENT EDUCATION
Treatment Explanation: We thoroughly washed the wound to remove any tiny glass fragments and used stitches to pull the skin edges perfectly together. This stops the bleeding, blocks bacteria, and ensures the smallest possible scar.
Actionable Steps: Keep the dressing completely dry for 48 hours. Take regular paracetamol tonight for the pain. Do not lift anything heavy with your left arm until the stitches are removed in 7 to 10 days.

